fluxland: port from wlroots 0.18 to wlroots 0.20 (for kflux)

Applies to ecliptik/fluxland 32d1009 (v1.1.0). Same content as the eight commits
on branch wlroots-0.20 in third_party/fluxland (see docs/upstream/fluxland-pr.md).

Build:
- meson: depend on wlroots-0.20; drop the include/ directory that upstream
  references but never committed (setup fails on a clean clone).

API changes (wlroots 0.19 and 0.20 release notes):
- wlr_xdg_surface_get_geometry() removed: read wlr_xdg_surface.geometry.
- wlr_presentation_create() takes a protocol version (2).
- wlr_surface_accepts_tablet_v2() argument order swapped.
- wlr_xwayland_surface_set_maximized() takes one flag per axis.
- text-input-v3 / input-method-v2 manager signals renamed to new_text_input /
  new_input_method.
- wlr_drm_lease_v1.n_connectors removed (log line only).

Behaviour changes that compile but abort at runtime:
- No configure may be scheduled before a toplevel's initial commit: set the
  xdg-decoration mode from the first commit when the client creates the
  decoration early (every client using xdg-decoration crashed fluxland).
  Likewise only (de)activate toplevels that are initialized: wlroots resets
  an xdg surface on unmap, and focusing the next window on close crashed.
- No listeners may remain on a global's signals when it is destroyed: remove
  the xwayland, xdg-shell, xdg-decoration and gamma-control listeners before
  teardown (fluxland aborted on exit).

Fluxbox behaviour fixes found while testing in kflux (not wlroots related):
- Drag-to-tab: hit-test the drop target with the dragged window hidden; it
  follows the pointer, so drops only worked onto windows stacked above it.
  Activate the dropped tab, so keyboard focus is not left on a hidden tab.
- toolbar.tools: accept Fluxbox's comma-separated list, not only spaces.
- Icon bar: leave out windows docked in the slit.

Tests: test_rules stubbed the removed geometry getter; set the field instead.
test_toolbar_layout's wm_view stub gains `docked`.
The other unit tests stub wlroots 0.18's API and are not ported.

